From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joshua Warren <816217+joshuaswarren@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 19:11:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 08/12] arm64: dts: apple: t6050-k114-k116: give the MTP DART
 streams 0 and 1 to the transport

With the MTP receive ring enabled on a K114c, the coprocessor wrote the ring
over DART stream 1 while the transport listed stream 0 only. The DART reported
"translation fault: SID:1 write BPF reject" at the ring address, the
coprocessor crashed with a DMA error, and the keyboard and trackpad stopped.

List both streams on the HID transport. apple_dart_device_group() needs every
stream of a device in one IOMMU group, and the MTP helper shares stream 0 with
the transport. With the helper on stream 0 only, the DART probe failed with
-22 on a K114c boot, so the helper lists both streams too. The helper's list is
set here, for the K114 and K116 boards, and not in t6050-max.dtsi, so other
T6050 boards keep stream 0 only.

Nothing in the base uses stream 1 yet; the ring driver change is a separate PR.

Signed-off-by: Joshua Warren <816217+joshuaswarren@users.noreply.github.com>
(cherry picked from commit 0d1408c7df796287c43a3dc62bf85e0d7225e430)
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6050-k114-k116.dtsi | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6050-k114-k116.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6050-k114-k116.dtsi
index 2fa146288f..0a4ca91798 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6050-k114-k116.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6050-k114-k116.dtsi
@@ -190,6 +190,11 @@ &fpwm2 {
 	status = "disabled";
 };
 
+/* The helper and its HID transport share one IOMMU group, so both list streams 0 and 1. */
+&mtp {
+	iommus = <&mtp_dart 0>, <&mtp_dart 1>;
+};
+
 /*
  * The keyboard, trackpad and touchscreen: the HID transport on the MTP's
  * DockChannel FIFO, laid out as on J716c (ADT dockchannel-mtp/mtp-transport).
@@ -200,7 +205,11 @@ mtp_hid: input@8000 {
 		reg = <0x8000 0x1000>, <0xc000 0x1000>,
 		      <0x0 0x1000>, <0x4000 0x1000>;
 		reg-names = "config", "data", "rmt-config", "rmt-data";
-		iommus = <&mtp_dart 0>;
+		/*
+		 * The coprocessor writes the MTP receive ring over DART stream 1. Both
+		 * streams must be in one IOMMU group, so the helper lists the same two.
+		 */
+		iommus = <&mtp_dart 0>, <&mtp_dart 1>;
 		interrupt-parent = <&mtp_dockchannel>;
 		interrupts = <2 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,
 			     <3 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
-- 
